 do.edu/api/v1/courses/138441/modules/967837" data-api-returntype="Module">
 Homework</a></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Cheating on homework cheats students out of de
 veloping the knowledge\, skills\, and ability gained from taking ECEN 2250
  and will only serve to make subsequent course content too challenging to 
 understand and complete. Courses that use ECEN 2250 as a prerequisite will
  then become extremely stressful because the student does not have the pre
 requisite knowledge to apply to more challenging situations. Avoid this si
 tuation by putting in the time to learn the material. The homework should 
 take time and be challenging\, it should be hard to understand\, that is w
 hy you are taking the course\, because it is not simple.</li>\n<li>Tips fo
 r doing well on the weekly homework and in this course: always attend lect
 ure\, ask questions during lecture\, read the textbook both before lecture
  and after lecture\, do practice problems from lecture\, quizzes\, and the
  textbook. Attend office hours and ask questions\, create problems for oth
 er students in the course and practice solving the problems\, talk about t
