DESCRIPTION:All labs must be typed.\n\nHandwritten labs will result in ZERO
  credit!\n\n* Submit online via Canvas by uploading single pdf\, make sure
  to name the file accordingly\, eg ECEN2250_Lab1\n\n* Scan color 300 dpi i
 nto a single easily readable pdf\, no credit for multiple pdfs\n\n* Make i
 t easy for the grader to grade\, if the grader can't read it\, then they c
 an't grade it and will not give any credit\n\n* Keep a copy of your work\n
 \n* Make sure that when you submit lab that it is submitted properly\, it 
 is the students responsibility\, no exceptions.\n\n* No late work beyond 2
 4 hours late will be accepted (except in cases of documented emergencies o
 r previous arrangements). (With prior approval of late submission) When su
 bmitting late work\, use Canvas\, if the Canvas Assignment is closed\, the
 n submit it via email using your @colorado.edu account and send it to both
  Arielle ([amblum@colorado.edu] (mailto:amblum@colorado.edu)) AND ALL of t
 he LAs with the assignment attached to the email\, email title = 'ECEN 225
 0 - Late Lab Submission #<Insert lab Number> <Insert Your Name>'\n\n* The 
 Labs will build from the previous week’s work\, so it is essential that 
 students do the lab every week\, otherwise students will be lost in the co
 urse. \n\n* Students are responsible for ensuring that their .pdf file up
 loaded properly for the submission by downloading their pdf after submitti
 ng the assignment to verify that there are no issues\, the pdf is readable
 \, the written work is legible and the file is not corrupted or too large.
  Failure to do so will result in the student receiving NO CREDIT for the a
 ssignment submission if there are any issues as outlined above.\n\n* See t
 he Syllabus for additional details.\n\n[Labs] (https://canvas.colorado.edu
 /courses/138441/modules/967838)\n\nAll supplemental videos can be found on
  Canvas > Modules > [Video Modules] (https://canvas.colorado.edu/courses/1
 38441/modules/967843) \n\n* Cheating on labs cheats students out of devel
 oping the knowledge\, skills\, and ability gained from taking ECEN 2250 an
 d will only serve to make subsequent course content too challenging to und
 erstand and complete. Courses that use ECEN 2250 as a prerequisite will th
 en become extremely stressful because the student does not have the prereq
 uisite knowledge to apply to more challenging situations. Avoid this situa
 tion by putting in the time to learn the material. The lab should take tim
 e and be challenging\, it should be hard to understand\, that is why you a
 re taking the course\, because it is not simple.\n\n* Tips for doing well 
 on the weekly labs and in this course: always attend lecture\, ask questio
 ns during lecture\, read the textbook both before lecture and after lectur
 e\, do practice problems from lecture\, quizzes\, and the textbook. Attend
  office hours and ask questions\, create problems for other students in th
 e course and practice solving the problems\, talk about the concepts with 
 other students\, help other students who are struggling. Make flash card o
 n basic topics and practice them. Go to office hours to ask questions abou
 t any differences.\n\n* Invest time\, energy\, and effort into your educat
 ion.
