URL;VALUE=URI:https://canvas.colorado.edu/calendar?include_contexts=course_
 138441&month=10&year=2026#assignment_2775873
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<link rel="stylesheet" href="https://instructu
 re-uploads.s3.amazonaws.com/account_107720000000000001/attachments/7403587
 6/dp_app.css"><p>All labs must be typed.</p>\n<p>Handwritten labs will res
 ult in ZERO credit!</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Submit online via Canvas by uploading <
 strong>single </strong>pdf\, make sure to name the file accordingly\, eg E
 CEN2250_Lab1</li>\n<li>Scan color 300 dpi into a single easily readable pd
 f\, <strong>no credit for multiple pdfs</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<ul>\n<li>Ma
 ke it easy for the grader to grade\, if the grader can't read it\, then th
 ey can't grade it and will not give any credit</li>\n<li>Keep a copy of yo
 ur work</li>\n<li>Make sure that when you submit lab that it is submitted 
 properly\, it is the students responsibility\, no exceptions.</li>\n<li>No
  late work beyond 24 hours late will be accepted (except in cases of docum
 ented emergencies or previous arrangements). (With prior approval of late 
 submission) When submitting late work\, use Canvas\, if the Canvas Assignm
 ent is closed\, then submit it via email using your @colorado.edu account 
 and send it to both Arielle (<a href="mailto:amblum@colorado.edu">amblum@c
 olorado.edu</a>) AND ALL of the LAs with the assignment attached to the em
 ail\, email title = 'ECEN 2250 - Late Lab Submission #&lt\;Insert lab Numb
 er&gt\; &lt\;Insert Your Name&gt\;'</li>\n<li>The Labs will build from the
  previous week’s work\, so it is essential that students do the lab ever
 y week\, otherwise students will be lost in the course.&nbsp\;</li>\n<li><
 span style="background-color: #fbeeb8\;">Students are responsible for ensu
 ring that their .pdf file uploaded properly for the submission by download
 ing their pdf after submitting the assignment to verify that there are no 
 issues\, the pdf is readable\, the written work is legible and the file is
  not corrupted or too large. Failure to do so will result in the student r
 eceiving NO CREDIT for the assignment submission if there are any issues a
 s outlined above.</span></li>\n<li>See the Syllabus for additional details
 .</li>\n</ul>\n<p><a title="Labs" href="https://canvas.colorado.edu/course
 s/138441/modules/967838" data-course-type="modules" data-published="true" 
 data-api-endpoint="https://canvas.colorado.edu/api/v1/courses/138441/modul
 es/967838" data-api-returntype="Module">Labs</a></p>\n<p style="padding-le
 ft: 40px\;">All supplemental videos can be found on Canvas &gt\; Modules &
 gt\; <a title="Video Modules" href="https://canvas.colorado.edu/courses/13
 8441/modules/967843" data-api-endpoint="https://canvas.colorado.edu/api/v1
 /courses/138441/modules/967843" data-api-returntype="Module">Video Modules
 </a>&nbsp\;</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Cheating on labs cheats students out of develop
 ing the knowledge\, skills\, and ability gained from taking ECEN 2250 and 
 will only serve to make subsequent course content too challenging to under
 stand and complete. Courses that use ECEN 2250 as a prerequisite will then
  become extremely stressful because the student does not have the prerequi
 site knowledge to apply to more challenging situations. Avoid this situati
 on by putting in the time to learn the material. The lab should take time 
 and be challenging\, it should be hard to understand\, that is why you are
  taking the course\, because it is not simple.</li>\n<li>Tips for doing we
 ll on the weekly labs and in this course: always attend lecture\, ask ques
 tions during lecture\, read the textbook both before lecture and after lec
 ture\, do practice problems from lecture\, quizzes\, and the textbook. Att
 end office hours and ask questions\, create problems for other students in
  the course and practice solving the problems\, talk about the concepts wi
 th other students\, help other students who are struggling. Make flash car
 d on basic topics and practice them. Go to office hours to ask questions a
 bout any differences.</li>\n<li>Invest time\, energy\, and effort into you
 r education.</li>\n</ul><script src="https://instructure-uploads.s3.amazon
 aws.com/account_107720000000000001/attachments/74035875/dp_app.js"></scrip
 t>
END:VEVENT
