DESCRIPTION:Download your performance lab code from GitHub.\n\n------------
 -----------------------------------\n\nIMPORTANT: The interview grading si
 gn-up slots will be posted during the week of the lab deadline. The sign-u
 p deadline is the same as the lab deadline.\n-----------------------------
 --------------------------------------------------------------------------
 -------------------------------------------------\n\n \n\nThe readme for 
 the lab is available in your repository.\n\nThis assignment deals with opt
 imizing memory-intensive code. Image processing offers many examples of fu
 nctions that can benefit from optimization. In this lab\, you’ll be impr
 oving the overall performance of an “image processing” application by 
 a factor of about 25 – an extra credit phase will challenge you to incre
 ase the speed further.\n\nThis lab uses GitHub actions to grade your lab 
 performance. Every time you commit and push your changes to Github\, the c
 ode will run on a specific computer with 2 cores. You can get the "Actions
 " tab of your GitHub repository to determine the score. While you can deve
 lop the code on any machine you like\, the evaluation will be done using t
 hese specific computers. You can get more information about the processor 
 model\, the cache size(s)\, and the specific features of that machine by l
 ooking at the cat /proc/cpuinfo action from a run. You can determine you
 r score by looking at the last ./Judge action.
