 6/dp_app.css"><div title="Page 1">\n<div>\n<div>\n<h3><span><strong>Downlo
 ad your performance lab code from GitHub.</strong><br></span></h3>\n<h3><s
 trong>IMPORTANT: The interview grading sign-up slots will be posted during
  the week of the lab deadline. The sign-up deadline is the same as the lab
  deadline.</strong></h3>\n<p>&nbsp\;</p>\n<p><span>The readme for the lab 
 is available in your repository.</span></p>\n<p>This assignment deals with
  optimizing memory-intensive code. Image processing offers many examples o
 f functions that can benefit from optimization. In this lab\, you’ll be 
 improving the overall performance of an “image processing” application
  by a factor of about 25 – an extra credit phase will challenge you to i
 ncrease the speed further.</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<p><span>This lab 
 uses </span><em>GitHub actions</em><span>&nbsp\;to grade your lab performa
 nce. Every time you commit and push your changes to Github\, the code will
  run on a specific computer with 2 cores. You can get the "Actions" tab of
  your GitHub repository to determine the score. While you can develop the 
 code on any machine you like\, the evaluation will be done using these spe
