DESCRIPTION:*\n\n* Submit online via Canvas by uploading single pdf\, make 
 sure to name the file accordingly\, eg ECEN2250_Homework4\n\n* Scan B&W at
  150-300 dpi into a single easily readable pdf\, no credit for multiple pd
 fs\n\n* Write the problem number and box your answer\, make it easy for th
 e grader to grade\, if the grader can't read it\, then they can't grade it
  and will not give any credit\n\n* Keep a copy of your work\n\n* Make sure
  that when you submit homework that it is submitted properly\, it is the s
 tudents responsibility\, no exceptions.\n\n* No late work beyond 24 hours 
 late will be accepted (except in cases of documented emergencies or previo
 us arrangements). (With prior approval of late submission) When submitting
  late work\, use Canvas\, if the Canvas Assignment is closed\, then submit
  it via email using your @colorado.edu account and send it to both Arielle
  ([amblum@colorado.edu] (mailto:amblum@colorado.edu)) AND ALL of the LAs w
 ith the assignment attached to the email\, email title = 'ECEN 2250 - Late
  Homework Submission <Insert Your Name>'\n\n* The homework will builds fro
 m the previous week’s work\, so it is essential that students do the hom
 ework every week\, otherwise students will be lost in the course. \n\n* S
 tudents are responsible for ensuring that their .pdf file uploaded properl
 y for the submission by downloading their pdf after submitting the assignm
 ent to verify that there are no issues\, the pdf is readable\, the written
  work is legible and the file is not corrupted or too large. Failure to do
  so will result in the student receiving NO CREDIT for the assignment subm
 ission if there are any issues as outlined above.\n\n* See the Syllabus fo
 r additional details.\n\n[Homework] (https://canvas.colorado.edu/courses/1
 38441/modules/967837)\n\n* Cheating on homework cheats students out of dev
 eloping the knowledge\, skills\, and ability gained from taking ECEN 2250 
 and will only serve to make subsequent course content too challenging to u
 nderstand and complete. Courses that use ECEN 2250 as a prerequisite will 
 then become extremely stressful because the student does not have the prer
 equisite knowledge to apply to more challenging situations. Avoid this sit
 uation by putting in the time to learn the material. The homework should t
 ake time and be challenging\, it should be hard to understand\, that is wh
 y you are taking the course\, because it is not simple.\n\n* Tips for doin
 g well on the weekly homework and in this course: always attend lecture\, 
 ask questions during lecture\, read the textbook both before lecture and a
 fter lecture\, do practice problems from lecture\, quizzes\, and the textb
 ook. Attend office hours and ask questions\, create problems for other stu
 dents in the course and practice solving the problems\, talk about the con
 cepts with other students\, help other students who are struggling. Make f
 lash card on basic topics and practice them. When homework solutions are r
 eleased\, go over them and compare them with your solutions and make sure 
 you understand any differences\, go to office hours to ask questions about
  any differences.\n\n* Invest time\, energy\, and effort into your educati
 on.
