 d this situation by putting in the time to learn the material. The homewor
 k should take time and be challenging\, it should be hard to understand\, 
 that is why you are taking the course\, because it is not simple.</li>\n<l
 i>Tips for doing well on the weekly homework and in this course: always at
 tend lecture\, ask questions during lecture\, read the textbook both befor
 e lecture and after lecture\, do practice problems from lecture\, quizzes\
 , and the textbook. Attend office hours and ask questions\, create problem
 s for other students in the course and practice solving the problems\, tal
 k about the concepts with other students\, help other students who are str
 uggling. Make flash card on basic topics and practice them. When homework 
 solutions are released\, go over them and compare them with your solutions
  and make sure you understand any differences\, go to office hours to ask 
 questions about any differences.</li>\n<li>Invest time\, energy\, and effo
 rt into your education.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul><script src="https://inst
 ructure-uploads.s3.amazonaws.com/account_107720000000000001/attachments/74
 035875/dp_app.js"></script>
END:VEVENT
